ng, with two copies that see different inputs. The other copy's function node takes a different input, so intervening on my copy's function shouldn't reach its act. Since that act is computed on a separate input, I don't see an edge between them, and I'm checking what follows from that.\n\nI've settled on defection as the fixed point under A-FDT: with the other copy held fixed, defecting gives the better payoff in each case, and cooperation isn't self-consistent. That's the essay's split-coordination result. Since the instructions say to use A-FDT as interpreted, I'll submit the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working under the A-FDT reading, with two copies that see different inputs. The other copy's function node takes a different input, so intervening on my copy's function shouldn't reach its act. Since that act is computed on a separate input, I don't see an edge between them, and I'm checking what follows from that.\n\nI've settled on defection as the fixed point under A-FDT: with the other copy held fixed, defecting gives the better payoff in each case, and cooperation isn't self-consistent. That's the essay's split-coordination result. Since the instructions say to use A-FDT as interpreted, I'll submit the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10148,"completion_tokens":885,"total_tokens":11033,"cost":0.058292,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.058292,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040592,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0177},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":349,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}